    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d807">

                <pb facs="0870" n="858" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg858"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/756½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé of the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gromyko</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President Roosevelt
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-07">November 7,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: On behalf of the Union
                    of Soviet Socialist Republics, pursuant to Sections 4 and 7 of the Lend-Lease
                    Act of March 11, 1941, I hereby represent that: <list>
                        <label>1)</label>
                        <item>Every contract or agreement for the disposition of any defense article
                            or defense information, pursuant to Section 3 of the Act of March 11,
                            1941, to the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics shall be <pb
                                facs="0871" n="859" xml:id="pg859"/> deemed to include a clause that
                            such government will not, without your consent, or the consent of
                            someone designated by you for that purpose, under the Act, transfer
                            title to or possession of such defense article or defense information by
                            gift, sale, or otherwise, or permit its use by anyone not an officer,
                            employee or agent of the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics; and</item>
                        <label>2)</label>
                        <item>If, as a result of the transfer to the Union of Soviet Socialist
                            Republics of any defense articles or defense information, it is
                            necessary, pursuant to Section 7 of the Act of March 11, 1941, fully to
                            protect the rights of any citizen of the United States, who has patent
                            rights in and to any such defense article or information, the Union of
                            Soviet Socialist Republics will do so, when so requested by you or your
                            designee for that purpose.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gromyko</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
